# Reverse proxy + automatic HTTPS (Let's Encrypt) for Grudge - frontend and
# backend both served from this one server (confirmed - see CLAUDE.md S3).
# Replace grudge.example.com below with the real subdomain once picked (see
# ../README.md). Caddy's reverse_proxy handles WebSocket upgrades
# automatically - no extra config needed for /ws/matchmaking, /ws/sim-rooms,
# /ws/tournaments.
#
# Two web addresses on the same server, not one - the backend keeps its own
# subdomain (api.grudge.example.com) rather than sharing a path prefix like
# /api on the frontend's own address. The backend's routes aren't all under
# one shared prefix (e.g. /auth/google/login, /me, /automata, /friends all
# sit at the root), so a path-based split would mean hand-listing every
# backend route in this file and keeping it in sync forever - a second
# subdomain needs zero backend/frontend code changes and can't drift out of
# sync. Both DNS records point at the same server IP; Caddy tells them apart
# by which hostname the request came in on.

grudge.example.com {
	root * /opt/grudge/frontend/dist
	file_server
	try_files {path} /index.html
}

api.grudge.example.com {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8000
}
